Apple is expanding its partnership with the <a href="https://www.savethemusic.org/">Save The Music Foundation</a>, a non-profit organization dedicated to supporting music education in U.S. public schools. The organization donates musical instruments and technology to schools and much more.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/03/Logic-Pro-iPad-Lifestyle.jpg" alt="" width="1920" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1041042" /><br/>
"We're thrilled to be expanding our partnership with Save the Music, bringing music education to even more schools across the country," <a href="https://x.com/tim_cook/status/2033881798141481030">said</a> Apple CEO Tim Cook.<br/>
<br/>
Apple's expanded partnership will help to bring music programming to nearly 50 more schools.<br/>
<br/>
Cook visited the Wadleigh Secondary School for the Performing and Visual Arts in New York City to listen to music created by students there. In a short video, the students can be seen using Apple products like the iPad, Apple Pencil, and AirPods Max.<br/>
